# Standard macOS Host installer

Branch: `macos-installer`, starting at main e7121a2.

Goal: open one signed, notarized PKG in Installer, approve administrator access,
and install the Host without Terminal, Python, Xcode or Command Line Tools on
the destination Mac. macOS 27/Apple Silicon only. macOS privacy consent remains
explicit and cannot be granted by this installer.

1. Verify Developer ID Application and Developer ID Installer private-key
   identities on the dedicated development Mac. Never use the Mac App Store
   installer identity for this package. Keep notarization credentials in Keychain.
2. Use Bash preinstall/postinstall scripts and a shared script, executed only
   by Installer as root. No custom installer executable, transaction framework,
   downloadable runtime, Python, AppleScript or persistent installer helper.
   Retain configuration, private identities, protected log creation, bounded
   graphical-worker/coordinator drain, and system-wide LoginWindow/Aqua startup.
3. Use ordinary payload/receipt-based PKG installation to /Applications. Reject
   alternate volumes, unsupported OS/architecture, unsafe filesystem objects,
   unrelated existing apps/jobs and signer mismatch before stopping services.
   Recovery is reinstalling the signed package; do not accumulate old app copies.
   The deliberate Apple Development to
   same-team Developer ID transition needs explicit permission continuity tests;
   do not silently claim existing TCC grants survive it.
4. Sign the app with hardened runtime and a secure timestamp, sign the installer
   with Developer ID Installer, notarize and staple the final PKG. Keep the
   production download unavailable until signature/notarization gates pass.
5. Test script failure paths without changing services, inspect package payload,
   scripts, version and signatures, then obtain authorization to exercise real
   install/upgrade on development-mac. Never interrupt its session or reboot automatically.
   Test fresh-machine absence of Python/developer tools and permission workflow.
6. Install a self-contained `Contents/Resources/uninstall.sh` in the signed
   Host app, invoked with sudo, retaining bounded shutdown and preserved
   settings/certificates/logs. Do not generate a separate uninstall PKG or
   present the Python development uninstaller as the production workflow.
7. Set the Host payload's native Installer conclusion to `RecommendRestart`.
   Explain that restarting loads updated microphone drivers and completes any
   pending camera extension updates. Remind users to save work and allow them
   to defer; installer scripts must not reboot the Mac or restart Core Audio.
   Query the finished package's `RestartAction` before notarization. The macOS
   packaging fixture also checks this action without installing its payload.

Reference inspection: Anyware Graphics Agent26.05.3 is a Developer ID-signed,
notarized PKG with Bash pre/postinstall scripts, payload launchd entries and a
compiled uninstaller. It delegates privacy prompts to its user agent; its
scripts do not automatically grant TCC consent. Adopt the standard packaging
structure, not its proprietary code, legacy cleanup, account creation,
firewall changes, CoreAudio restart or timed permission-prompt loops.
Reference PKG SHA-256:
`7250bf5a3117fc2370ec9fda9d1529e64cd6499202b35c59b7b1ee7346b660cd`.
The reference Mac was read-only; extraction was on the dedicated development Mac.

Current checkpoint: the user explicitly retained signing/notarization and
approved replacing the first native-helper implementation with simple scripts.
Both Developer ID identities and Keychain profile `plank-notary` are provisioned.
Historical checkpoint: installer and uninstaller1.0.80-macos-installer were built, signed,
notarized (Accepted), stapled and Gatekeeper-verified. Shell tests pass19 on Mac
and29 with the isolated root filesystem fixture. Installed-app read-only
preflight, package payload/scripts/version and Installer metadata pass.
Exact artifacts/source/hashes are in HANDOFF. No installed Host, permissions or streaming code changed.
Live install/upgrade/uninstall, fresh-machine and permission continuity gates
remain open. Uninstall removes app, launchd entries and the Host receipt while
preserving configuration, keys, logs and privacy approvals.
